# NOTES
- Systematic pattern observed across many plants: the guessed "constructor" field appears to have been populated with the NSSS/reactor vendor name (GE, Westinghouse, CE, B&W) rather than the actual general contractor/builder. Where a distinct general contractor could be sourced (Elk River -> Maxon Construction, Farley -> Fluor Corporation, Fitzpatrick -> Niagara Mohawk (owner-built), Fermi 1 -> Power Reactor Development Co., Hallam -> Atomics International, Haddam Neck -> Stone & Webster, Diablo Canyon -> Fluor Corporation (LOW confidence, single trade-press source), GE Vallecitos AE -> Bechtel), it was marked WRONG. This suggests the original heuristic guess for "constructor" was systematically derived from the reactor/NSSS vendor column rather than independent research, across the whole dataset, not just this batch.
- rpv_manufacturer is the weakest-sourced field overall: for nearly every plant, only the NSSS/reactor vendor is documented in accessible sources (Wikipedia infoboxes, WNA), and no source distinguishes a separate vessel fabricator. Most rpv_manufacturer rows are UNVERIFIABLE as a result — the guessed values (often Combustion Engineering as fabricator for GE/Westinghouse-designed plants) could not be confirmed OR refuted with available sources.
- turbine_supplier for Fermi 2 and Fitzpatrick was originally General Electric in the guessed data; sourced fact is that BOTH plants originally had English Electric turbines, replaced by GE only after 1993 turbine-blade failures at Fermi 2/similar era issues. Guessed value may reflect current-state hardware rather than as-built supplier — worth checking if other GE BWR plants in the full dataset have the same as-built vs. current-state ambiguity.
- Wikipedia's standard power-station infobox template does not carry constructor/architect-engineer/turbine-supplier/RPV-fabricator fields for most of these 1960s-1980s plants (only "reactor supplier," i.e., NSSS vendor) — this is why a large share of fields across Harris, Hatch, Hope Creek, Humboldt Bay, Ginna, Fort Calhoun, Fort St. Vrain, Farley (turbine/RPV) came back UNVERIFIABLE rather than confirmed. Primary NRC FSAR/docket documents were largely inaccessible (403 errors) or not reached before per-agent WebSearch budgets (200 calls) were exhausted. A follow-up pass with direct NRC ADAMS/FSAR PDF access or IAEA PRIS (which has explicit Constructor/Turbine Supplier fields) would likely resolve many of these.
- Fort Calhoun: guessed turbine_supplier = General Electric despite the plant being a Combustion Engineering NSSS design — flagged as a plausible mismatch but could not be confirmed or refuted; left UNVERIFIABLE rather than guessing.
